#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Balance as JSON: every balance table of the game, read into JSON and written back (docs/reference/combat.md).

Three layers, merged in this order:
  original   the player's own disc (extracted/): never committed; `extract` writes it to build/balance/original/
  engine     content/balance/engine/tables.json: what the C patch series changes in those tables (generated by
             `sync` from a built executable; committed, the mod's own values; do not edit by hand)
  overrides  content/balance/*.json: hand-written balance changes (sparse, same layout), and ids >= 180 too
             (applied by species.py when it builds DIGI.DAT)

`build` reads only the executable it is given: for a compiled one its own tables are the floor (they are original +
engine layer, which is what the C initializes), then the species files and the committed JSON. It never opens the USA
executable or overlays of extracted/, so any release's disc can be the base. `extract`, `verify`, `sync`, `check`, `dump`
and `show` are developer tools that still read the USA executable (the original layer); `verify` and `check` are where
a C patch that changed a table after the last `sync` shows up.

Usage:
  balance.py extract [-o build/balance/original]          original values (tables.json, maps.json) from extracted/
  balance.py verify  [--exe-dir DIR]                      original + engine == the tables of the build (the proof)
  balance.py sync    [--exe-dir DIR]                      regenerate the engine layer from a build
  balance.py check   [--exe-dir DIR]                      validate the overrides (keys, ranges, references)
  balance.py build   --exe-dir DIR -o OUT [--file DEST=SRC ...] [--no-maps]
                                                          OUT/ = the build's executable and overlays with every
                                                          table written from JSON, OUT/maps/... patched .MAP files
                                                          ("FILE: DEST=SRC" lines for build-disc.py --file);
                                                          --no-maps: the tables only (tools/build-full.sh: the maps
                                                          are tools/derive's balance step, build_maps())
  balance.py dump    [--exe-dir DIR] [-o build/balance/effective.json]
                                                          what the game will use: every layer merged, every
                                                          species (ids >= 180 from content/species) in one layout
  balance.py show ID [--exe-dir DIR]                      one species, effective values

DIR is a compiled executable's folder (SLUS_010.32 + SLUS_010.32.elf + *_REL.BIN), default
build/decomp-int/build/us/psx/gcc. A folder without the .elf is taken as the original executable (no engine
layer): a balance mod for the unmodified game.
Keys starting with "_" are comments (the dumps use them for names) and are ignored everywhere.
"""
